---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../../components/GradientText.astro";
import PlayableNav from "../../components/PlayableNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Release Quality & Platform Readiness | Aniloom Technologies" description="Playable ad QA starting at $1,500 USD: one playable, portrait and landscape, up to two variants, one provider package, findings, one retest, and a release summary.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <PlayableNav />
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Release Quality & Platform Readiness</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>A QA package for your <GradientText>existing playable.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>Starting at $1,500 USD. We test one stable playable and deliver prioritized findings, one retest after corrections, and a release-readiness summary. Engineering fixes are separate scope.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open data-contact-topic="Playable Release Quality and Platform Readiness">Discuss the package</button><a class="text-link" href="#package">See what is included <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry-points section-shell section-pad" id="package">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Base package</p><h2>What is included.</h2></div><p>For a playable approaching delivery or launch, or a build changed by adaptation or corrections. The proposal confirms the exact specification and timeline.</p></div>
      <div class="entry-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>01</span><h2>One existing playable</h2><p>A stable build in portrait and landscape, with up to two behavioral variants and one ad-network provider package.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>02</span><h2>Testing and findings</h2><p>Risk mapping, visual and responsive checks, user-journey testing, variant and package review, and prioritized findings with evidence.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>03</span><h2>One retest and summary</h2><p>One retest after corrections, followed by a release-readiness summary of tested areas, open issues, and remaining risks.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band surface-dark section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Package steps</p><h2>From test scope to release summary.</h2></div><p>Plan for 3-5 business days after stable-build access. The final schedule depends on the scope, access, and corrections required.</p></div>
        <ol class="package-steps">
          <li data-reveal><span>01</span><div><h3>Confirm the test scope</h3><p>Agree on the build, variants, provider specification, acceptance criteria, and configurations to review.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>02</span><div><h3>Test the playable</h3><p>Check the interaction, visual presentation, orientations, variants, and provider package against the agreed scope.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>03</span><div><h3>Report issues</h3><p>Deliver prioritized findings with reproduction steps and evidence. Your developers prepare corrections, or we scope an engineering sprint separately.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>04</span><div><h3>Retest and summarize</h3><p>Recheck the corrected build once, then report resolved issues, open defects, untested areas, and remaining release risks.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverable section-shell section-pad">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Deliverables</p><h2>The reports you receive.</h2></div><p>The reports document what was tested and what still needs attention before the team makes its release decision.</p></div>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div data-reveal><span>Risk map and test scope</span><p>Priority interactions, orientations, variants, provider requirements, and configurations covered by the review.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Findings and evidence</span><p>Prioritized issue record with reproduction context, visual evidence, expected behavior, and current ownership.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Retest results</span><p>Findings rechecked after corrections, with resolved and still-open issues identified.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Release-readiness summary</span><p>Tested scope, open defects, blocked checks, and remaining risks for the team making the release decision.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-band section-shell" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Inputs and exclusions</p>
      <h2>What to provide before testing starts.</h2>
      <p>Provide stable-build access, the target provider specification, variants, known issues, and a decision-maker. Engineering fixes, extra providers or variants, localization, analytics validation, performance testing, and further retest rounds are separate scope.</p>
      <p>Testing supports a release decision. It does not certify the build or guarantee platform acceptance, campaign performance, or a defect-free release.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="service-crosslink section-shell" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Working examples</p><div><h2>Try three playable interactions.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/case-studies/magic-thai-playables/">Try the Magic Thai demos <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="callout surface-dark section-shell section-pad"><p class="eyebrow">Scope your review</p><h2>Bring the playable, target provider, and deadline.</h2><p>We will confirm whether this package fits and identify any additional testing or engineering work. Prices are in USD before applicable taxes.</p><div class="callout__actions"><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/pricing/">Compare packages and add-ons <span>↗</span></a><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open data-contact-topic="Playable Release Quality and Platform Readiness">Discuss the package</button></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
